The widget now shows more of your clocks before it hides any: it drops to compact rows first, and only then sets aside a zone whose time is already on screen. When anything is hidden it says so.

When two places keep the same time, the one you named — Mississauga rather than a bare zone — is the one that stays. Renaming a place that shares a zone with one you already saved now sticks.

A port of call carries its anchor on the widget too, when the row has room.
